# Varnish Module (VMOD) `object_mut`

```vcl
// Place import statement at the top of your VCL file
// This loads vmod from a standard location
import object_mut;

// Or load vmod from a specific file
import object_mut from "path/to/libobject_mut.so";
```

## Object `Counter`

### Constructor `object_mut.new()`

### Method `VOID <object>.set(INT value)`

**Restricted to:** `housekeeping`

Only callable from vcl_init and vcl_fini, so `&mut self` is allowed.

### Method `VOID <object>.add(INT value)`

**Restricted to:** `vcl_init`

### Method `VOID <object>.add_ws(INT value)`

**Restricted to:** `vcl_init`

### Method `VOID <object>.reset()`

**Restricted to:** `vcl_init`, `vcl_fini`

### Method `INT <object>.get()`

### Method `INT <object>.run(SUB sub)`

**Restricted to:** `client`, `backend`

`&mut Ctx` is fine on a `&self` method that can't run in vcl_init/vcl_fini.

### Method `INT <object>.run_client(SUB sub)`

**Restricted to:** `client`

### Method `INT <object>.run_backend(SUB sub)`

**Restricted to:** `backend`

### Method `INT <object>.get_ctx()`

`&Ctx` cannot call a VCL sub, so it is allowed in any scope.

